Subject: Keep low-address symbols in relocatable Mach-O objects

MH_OBJECT symbols use section-relative values and may legitimately start at
zero. Preserve the existing filter for linked images. Upstream removed this
filter in the broader symbol-loader refactor (3e812278b5b5126f9d03ed6a2da1ea24ea7ad0c1,
1920cca72517012a81d3ebafed7175da6b015be7); this is a local, narrow compatibility
fix for 5.8.2, not a backport of that parser rewrite.

--- a/libr/bin/p/bin_mach0.c
+++ b/libr/bin/p/bin_mach0.c
@@ -235,7 +235,8 @@
 	Sdb *symcache = sdb_new0 ();
 	bin = (struct MACH0_(obj_t) *) obj->bin_obj;
 	for (i = 0; !syms[i].last; i++) {
-		if (syms[i].name == NULL || syms[i].name[0] == '\0' || syms[i].addr < 100) {
+		if (syms[i].name == NULL || syms[i].name[0] == '\0' ||
+			(bin->hdr.filetype != MH_OBJECT && syms[i].addr < 100)) {
 			continue;
 		}
 		if (!(ptr = R_NEW0 (RBinSymbol))) {
